Third-party notices
===================

nmosyn/osc.py is a translation to Python (numba) of the algorithms of the two codes below: the eigenvalues and
eigenvectors of the Hamiltonian in matter from NuFast, and the amplitudes of layers of constant density and the
theta23 / delta_CP rotation from NuFast-Earth. Their licenses and copyright notices follow, as they require.

Please also cite:
  P. B. Denton and S. J. Parke, "Fast and Accurate Algorithm for Calculating Long-Baseline Neutrino Oscillation
  Probabilities with Matter Effects: NuFast", arXiv:2405.02400.
  P. B. Denton and S. J. Parke, "NuFast-Earth: Efficient Atmospheric, Solar, and Supernova Neutrino Propagation
  Through the Earth", Phys. Rev. D, arXiv:2511.04735.


